            <div xml:id="d162">

                <pb facs="0249" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3775: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-31T22:00:00+08:00">January 31, 1932—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 31—9:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My telegram January 30, 4 p.m. and Department’s January 30, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>2. The Secretary General of the Council informed me this afternoon that the
                    Council had decided not to file a formal protest against the violation of the
                    neutrality of the Settlement.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation and Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
